A||||4||MooCow||Just got back from Ed Parks.||||6||
Z||000000||MooCow||11-06-2000||10:58 PM||||Well I am back from visiting Ed Parks and let me say it was a blast.  As some of you know I went down there thinking that I wanted an auto Fiero, boy was I wrong.  The  one I was supposed to test drive was an 86 SE V6 auto and was not nearly as fast as my 4-speed.  I thought it would be close but no way.  Ed let me drive another Auto Fiero that had the same tranny but with a 3.4 installed. Let me tell you it was fast.  Then he let me drive his formula with an auto with a different gear ratio.  Finally I drove a 3.4 with a 4-speed stick that had a 4:10 gear ratio and loved it.  The front of the car nearly came off the ground when you punched it in first.  Not to mention I could squeel tires in 3rd!  I did not trade my car for the Auto one but am selling my car so next year I can get a GT and Ed is putting in a 3.4 with a 4:10 gear 4-speed for me.  If I would have had a ride home Ed would have bought my car. So my car is for sale in the mall.  If it doesn't sell then Ed may still buy it.  When I fugure out PIP I will show you some pics of this awsome 88 GT with a 3.8 II in it along with other pics.  Sorry for being so long just had to tell you how fun I had even after driving 12 hours one way this weekend.<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||6
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-06-2000||11:52 PM||||Cool! Hey Moo..tell me some more..I only live about 4 hours away and want to go. I hear hes got ALOT of Fieros for sale..what are the conditions and price ranges?||||reg||14
Z||000002||Raydar||11-07-2000||12:21 AM||||Okay. Ken's hooked!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Fiero Nirvana!<P>I could go to Ed's and wander around for days! You should go to the swap meet in April. You can probably sell/buy whatever your heart desires. Glad you made the trip. Ed is one of the most knowledgeable Fiero folks in the country. And a d@mn nice guy, too!<BR>MooCow, if I were you I'd put the 3.4 in YOUR car, along with the 4.10, if you <I>really</I> felt the need. You've already got a fully loaded SE. That's as good as you'll ever find in a GT, except for the fastback and 15" wheels, and maybe some leather interior stuff. Those can be added. Just takes a bit of "shopping", and a couple days of work. <BR>Just an opinion.<P>Raydar||||reg||14
Z||000003||MooCow||11-07-2000||09:15 AM||||He has cars on the left side of the factory which are for parts and can't be restored.  On the other side of the fastory he has around 75 cars that can be restored with minor work.  I knowthat he has an white 88GT fully loaded for sale I think he said around $4,000 and he let me drive it.<BR>I was tempted to change mine over since my interior is near mint but when I convert it to a GT and if someone hits me then I am out of luck and the insurance will only pay for the SE.  I am still tempted but will most likley buy a GT.  Well like I said before when I ever get PIP I have around 4 disks fool of pics.  So if anyone wants me to E-mail them a couple I will be glad to.<BR>And yes I am hooked  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>                            Thanks Ken||||reg||10
Z||000004||007DOUG||11-07-2000||12:00 PM||||MooCow:<P>Was the 3.4 4:10 the white coupe?<P>I drove that fiero last time I was there. My word thats a quick fiero.<P>I'll be at the Fiero Factory Nov. 15th for a 4:10 tranny/clutch in my 86 GT. <P>I'm gonna drive his little rocket again. He should charge for rides in that car.<P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
